ShotLedger — license map

Copyright (c) 2026 Jimisola Laursen

This repository contains works under more than one license. REUSE.toml
decides which license applies to which file and is authoritative; in
summary:

- backend/ — Elastic License 2.0. Text: LICENSES/Elastic-2.0.txt.
  Licensor notice: backend/LICENSE.

- shared/src/sync/ — Apache License 2.0: the sync protocol and the Drizzle
  tables the backend compiles in. Text: LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

- Everything else, including app/ and the rest of shared/ — GNU Affero
  General Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any later version.
  Text:
  LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt. It comes with the additional permissions
  under its section 7 in LICENSES/LicenseRef-ShotLedger-AGPL-Permissions.txt
  (conveying through app stores; combining with proprietary platform
  libraries such as Google ML Kit).

- Third-party components keep their own licenses. .claude/skills/old-coder/
  is vendored under MIT (its own LICENSE file). The dependencies bundled into
  the app are listed in app/src/constants/licenses.json and
  app/src/constants/native-licenses.ts.

In SPDX terms: backend/ is "Elastic-2.0"; shared/src/sync/ is "Apache-2.0";
the rest is "AGPL-3.0-or-later WITH LicenseRef-ShotLedger-AGPL-Permissions".

Commercial licenses: as the copyright holder, Jimisola Laursen also
licenses ShotLedger under separate commercial terms, for anyone who wants to
use it without the obligations of the licenses above. Those terms are agreed
case by case and are not part of this repository; they never withdraw the
public licenses above. See docs/adr/0023-dual-licensing-agpl-and-commercial.md.

Contributions: see CONTRIBUTING.md and CLA.md. The reasoning behind this map
is recorded in docs/adr/0017-license-map-and-business-model.md.
